{"item": "T-0317", "job": "adjudicate-t-0317", "kind": "ruling", "product": "asf", "text": "Disputed: whether the round-3 review still has a C list to answer, after the lane held worker/T-0317 BACK 'kind=review' three times running. Checked directly: none of the three reviews (1/2/3-t-0317.md) has a `## C` heading or any C-list content — `asf.evidence.review.c_items()` returns `[]` for all three, and each says in prose \"No C list — nothing found that blocks.\" The hold is a false positive of the lane's own tooling: `asf.reviews.verdict()` (asf/reviews.py:150-158) derives BOUNCE (read as CHANGES by asf/evidence/review.py) because its `missing()` check requires an exact normalized-string match between the table's row names and `CHECKLIST['code']`'s literal text, and the rows all three reviewers wrote (\"scope: the diff stays inside `writes:`\", \"acceptance tests byte-identical to the plan's\") are exactly what `asf/briefs/templates/review.md:10-15` itself instructs every reviewer to write — a drift between the checklist (added by T-0265/#135) and the template that was never reconciled. Rounds 1-2 additionally hit a hard table-parse fault from an unescaped `|` inside one evidence cell's grep pattern. This is not specific to T-0317: the same table wording bounces docs/reviews/1-b-0087.md, 1-b-0090.md, 1-b-0099.md and 1-b-0110.md identically. Overruled: there is no C list and no code defect — the diff, the tests, and the gate are exactly what three independent rounds each verified and approved; T-0317's footprint and content stand unchanged. Separately, round 2's carried-forward I-item (write_agents_file's `tools=()` rendering `\"tools\": []`, spec §2.1 vs §2.4's worked example) is also not a Task-1 defect — T4's acceptance text (docs/specs/f-0062.md:746) literally reads \"tools is the row's set minus deny_tools\", and asf/roles/launch.py:144 implements that formula exactly — but it stays open, unresolved, for whoever wires Task 4/5's launch to confirm the rendered agents file is read the way the runtime expects.", "ts": "2026-09-28T00:01:03Z"}
